@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-nouns`
IMPORT `g6-schedule-three`
IMPORT `g6-notice-and-hearing`
IMPORT `g6-amount`
IMPORT `g6-payment`
IMPORT `g6-warning`
IMPORT `g6-appeal-and-publication`

-- g6-tests-scenarios.l4: three whole proceedings run through the modules in the order the Law runs them, to show that the
-- rules compose.  Every expected value was worked by hand from the Hebrew and Interpretation Law s.10 before any run,
-- and the money by Fraction arithmetic outside L4.  The index series is invented (the sources give none), the same as
-- in g6-tests-amount.l4: known on 1 January 2025, 2026, 2027: 100.0, 101.7, 103.4.
--
-- Scenario A, a corporation that stays silent: a repeat violation of item (5) on 2 November 2026 (an earlier item (6)
--   violation on 15 December 2025 ended in a sanction; both contravene s.18(a)); the notice of intention is delivered on
--   20 December 2026 and no representations follow, so the notice is treated as a demand delivered when the 30 days of
--   s.43 end, on 19 January 2027; s.48's 30 days from it end on 18 February 2027; s.47(a) updates the amount at the notice
--   day (20 December 2026), so the 2026 amount applies: 40,000 x 1.017 = 40,680, and 40,680 + 40,680 = 81,360.
--   A payment on 19 February 2027 is late by one day and owes 81,360 + 100 + 20 = 81,480 on the figures the caller supplies.
-- Scenario B, an individual who was warned and went on: the first update year is 2028 (Chapter 6 commences late), so the
--   amount is as enacted, 20,000; the breach began on 10 February 2027 and continued to 2 June 2027: 3 months completed,
--   so 20,000 + 3 x 400 = 21,200 (20,800 if the months are counted from the warning's delivery on 3 March, 2 months).
-- Scenario C, an appeal: a decision notified on Wednesday 2 June 2027; appeal by Saturday 17 July 2027; the court stays
--   payment and decides on 15 November 2027, which fixes the update day (the 2027 amount, 20,680); the sanction is
--   reduced to 15,000 after payment of 20,680, so 5,680 comes back, and with the shekel interest of 60, 5,740.

§ `Tests of whole proceedings`

§§ `Fixtures`

`a corporate violator`   MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "P-CORP", `kind of person` IS `a corporation`
`an individual violator` MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "P-IND", `kind of person` IS `an individual`

`violation (1)` MEANS `work with no licence at all`
`violation (5)` MEANS `engaging a person who had no licence at all`
`violation (6)` MEANS `engaging a person without a licence of the appropriate kind`

GIVEN who IS A Person
      item IS A `Listed violation`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A Violation
`a violation by` who `of` item `on` day MEANS
    Violation WITH `the violator` IS who
                 , `the listed violation` IS item
                 , `reference for the act` IS "act-1"
                 , `date of the act` IS day

`no day of rest at all` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS EMPTY

`the index readings` MEANS
    LIST (`Price index reading` OF 2024, 10, YMD 2024 11 15,  99.8)
       , (`Price index reading` OF 2024, 11, YMD 2024 12 15, 100.0)
       , (`Price index reading` OF 2024, 12, YMD 2025 1 15,  100.4)
       , (`Price index reading` OF 2025, 11, YMD 2025 12 15, 101.7)
       , (`Price index reading` OF 2025, 12, YMD 2026 1 15,  101.9)
       , (`Price index reading` OF 2026, 11, YMD 2026 12 15, 103.4)
       , (`Price index reading` OF 2026, 12, YMD 2027 1 15,  103.6)

-- Positional fields of `Notice of intention`: delivered on, in writing, act+date, amount, period (days), right,
-- deemed demand, power to add, intention to publish name.
`the complete notice delivered on 20 December 2026` MEANS `Notice of intention` OF YMD 2026 12 20, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, JUST 30, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE

§§ `Scenario A: a corporation, a repeat violation of item (5), silent after the notice`

`the corporation's item (5) violation of 2 November 2026` MEANS `a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (5)` `on` (YMD 2026 11 2)
-- Positional fields of `Previous violation`: violator, violation, date of the act, sanction imposed, convicted.
`the corporation's earlier item (6) violation, sanctioned` MEANS `Previous violation` OF `a corporate violator`, `violation (6)`, YMD 2025 12 15, TRUE, FALSE

-- It is a repeat (the same provision, s.18(a); within two years of 15 December 2025, to 15 December 2027).
#ASSERT `s 45(b) — the violation` `the corporation's item (5) violation of 2 November 2026` `is a repeat violation, given` (LIST `the corporation's earlier item (6) violation, sanctioned`)
-- The Commissioner may impose: Chapter 6 in force, the officer authorised, and a figure printed for a corporation at item (5).
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` `the corporation's item (5) violation of 2 November 2026` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for the violation` `the corporation's item (5) violation of 2 November 2026` EQUALS 40_000
-- Chapter 6 not yet in force on the day of the act: the Commissioner may not.
#ASSERT NOT `s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` `the corporation's item (5) violation of 2 November 2026` FALSE TRUE
-- The notice states what s.42(b) requires; no representations were made.
#ASSERT `s 42(b) — the notice of intention states what the Law requires` `the complete notice delivered on 20 December 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `s 43, s 44(d) — the violator made his representations within the period` `the complete notice delivered on 20 December 2026` NOTHING `no day of rest at all` NOTHING
-- The s.43 period ends on 19 January 2027, the notice is treated as a demand delivered then.
#ASSERT `s 43 — the last day for representations` `the complete notice delivered on 20 December 2026` NOTHING `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 19
#ASSERT `s 44 — the day the payment demand is delivered or treated as delivered` `the complete notice delivered on 20 December 2026` NOTHING FALSE NOTHING `no day of rest at all` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 1 19)
-- s.47(a): for a violator who made no representations, the day the notice was delivered.
#ASSERT `s 47(a) — the day on which the amount of the sanction is updated` (YMD 2026 12 20) FALSE (JUST (YMD 2027 1 19)) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 12 20)
-- The amount: 40,000 updated to 40,680 by the 2026 update, doubled by the repeat: 81,360.
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` `the corporation's item (5) violation of 2 November 2026` 0 TRUE (YMD 2026 12 20) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 81_360
-- s.48: 30 days from the deemed demand, 18 February 2027.
#ASSERT `s 48 — the last day of the 30 days from the delivery of the payment demand` (YMD 2027 1 19) `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 2 18
-- Paid on the last day: in time.  Paid the day after: late by one day.
#ASSERT NOT `s 49 — the payment of` (YMD 2027 2 18) `is late, the last day for payment being` (YMD 2027 2 18)
#ASSERT     `s 49 — the payment of` (YMD 2027 2 19) `is late, the last day for payment being` (YMD 2027 2 18)
#ASSERT `s 49 — the days of delay, from the day after` (YMD 2027 2 18) `until` (YMD 2027 2 19) EQUALS 1
-- The amount owed on the figures the caller supplies (100 shekel interest, 20 arrears fees): 81,480; without them the Law does not answer.
#ASSERT `s 49 — the amount owed on a sanction of` 81_360 `when the payment is late:` TRUE `with shekel interest` (JUST 100) `and arrears fees` (JUST 20) EQUALS 81_480
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 49 — the amount owed on a sanction of` 81_360 `when the payment is late:` TRUE `with shekel interest` NOTHING `and arrears fees` NOTHING
-- The duty as one rule: paid in full on 18 February (AT 30 from 19 January) is in time.
#TRACE `s 48 — the violator must pay the financial sanction of` 81_360 `, the demand being delivered on` (YMD 2027 1 19) `with` `no day of rest at all` `and, if late,` (JUST 100) `and` (JUST 20) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the violator` DOES `pay the financial sanction` `the violator` 81_360 AT 30

§§ `Scenario B: an individual warned for item (1), who went on breaching`

-- Positional fields of `Administrative warning`: violator, violation, delivered on, states act+date, tells to stop, warns,
-- states the right to ask for cancellation, cancelled.
`the warning of 3 March 2027` MEANS `Administrative warning` OF `an individual violator`, `violation (1)`, YMD 2027 3 3, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`the continued item (1) breach, begun on 10 February 2027` MEANS `a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2027 2 10)

#ASSERT `s 54(a) — a breach continued after` `the warning of 3 March 2027` `is treated as a continuing violation, the further breach being` `violation (1)` `and the violator having continued:` TRUE
-- The months: 3 completed from the day the breach began (10 March, 10 April, 10 May), 2 from the warning (3 April, 3 May).
#ASSERT `s 54(a) — the months of a continuing violation counted from the day the breach began` (YMD 2027 2 10) `until` (YMD 2027 6 2) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `s 54(a) — the months of a continuing violation counted from the delivery of` `the warning of 3 March 2027` `until` (YMD 2027 6 2) EQUALS 2
-- The sanction, the first update being in 2028 so that the amount is as enacted: 20,000 + 3 x 400 = 21,200 (20,800 for 2 months).
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` `the continued item (1) breach, begun on 10 February 2027` 3 FALSE (YMD 2027 6 2) 2028 `the index readings` EQUALS 21_200
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` `the continued item (1) breach, begun on 10 February 2027` 2 FALSE (YMD 2027 6 2) 2028 `the index readings` EQUALS 20_800
-- The Commissioner must give a notice of intention that states what s.42(b) requires.
#TRACE `s 54 — the Commissioner must give notice of intention after a warning` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `give the violator written notice of intention to impose a financial sanction after a warning` `the Commissioner` `the complete notice delivered on 20 December 2026` AT 20

§§ `Scenario C: an appeal, a stay, a reduction and a refund`

`the individual's item (1) violation of 1 March 2027` MEANS `a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)` `on` (YMD 2027 3 1)

-- The decision is notified on 2 June 2027; the appeal on 10 July is within the 45 days (to Saturday 17 July).
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — the last day of the 45 days from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `no day of rest at all` EQUALS YMD 2027 7 17
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 7 10) `is within the period to appeal that runs from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` `no day of rest at all`
-- The court orders a stay: execution is stayed (s.56(b)).
#ASSERT `s 56(b) — the filing of the appeal stays the execution of the decision, given` FALSE `and` TRUE
-- s.47(a): payment is stayed by the court, the appeal is decided on 15 November 2027, which is the update day.
#ASSERT `s 47(a) — the day on which the amount of the sanction is updated` (YMD 2027 3 3) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2027 6 2)) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2027 11 15)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 11 15)
-- The amount on that day: 20,000 updated twice (2026, 2027) is 20,680.
#ASSERT `s 45 to 47 — the financial sanction for the violation` `the individual's item (1) violation of 1 March 2027` 0 FALSE (YMD 2027 11 15) 2026 `the index readings` EQUALS 20_680
-- After payment of 20,680 the court reduces the sanction to 15,000: 5,680 comes back, and with the interest of 60, 5,740.
#ASSERT `s 56(c) — the amount to be returned of` 20_680 `when the court reduced the sanction to` (JUST 15_000) EQUALS 5_680
#ASSERT `s 56(c) — the amount returned with shekel interest` 5_680 `and` (JUST 60) EQUALS 5_740
-- The appeal is a fact the Commissioner must publish, with its result once there is one.
#TRACE `s 57(b) — the Commissioner must publish the appeal and its result` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `publish on the Ministry website that an appeal was filed and how it ended` `the Commissioner` TRUE TRUE AT 9
